[Term]
id: PR:000021997
name: TRK receptor
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that is a tyrosine kinase receptor that is activated by dimerization, resulting in autophosphorylation of intracellular tyrosine residues and triggering of the signal transduction cascade." [PMID:10388563]
comment: Category=family.
xref: PIRSF:PIRSF000623
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

[Term]
id: PR:000021998
name: neurotrophin
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that is a neurotrophic polypeptide factor that regulates neuronal differentiation and is essential for neuronal survival, neurite growth and plasticity. It contains a signal peptide, a propeptide, and a C-terminal Nerve growth factor family (Pfam:PF00243) domain." [PMID:10388563]
comment: Category=family.
xref: PIRSF:PIRSF001789
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

[Term]
id: PR:000021999
name: death receptor
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that contains multiple TNFR/NGFR cysteine-rich region (Pfam:PF00020) within the extracellular ligand-binding domain, a type I (single pass) transmembrane domain, and a cytoplasmic Death domain (Pfam:PF00531) required for intracellular signaling." [PMID:12655292]
comment: Category=family.
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

[Term]
id: PR:000022001
name: vertebrate G-type lysozyme
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that was initially identified as an antibacterial enzyme located in egg whites of Embden goose, but is now known to exist in both mammals and fish. Lysozyme catalyzes hydrolysis of most bacterial cell walls by cleaving the beta-1,4 glycosidic bond between N-acetyl-d-glucosamine (NAG) and N-acetylmuramic acid (NAM) in the peptidoglycan layer. It contains one copy of the Transglycosylase SLT domain (Pfam:PF01464)." [PMID:12574869]
comment: Category=family.
synonym: "goose-type lysozyme" EXACT []
xref: PIRSF:PIRSF001065
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

