[Term]
id: PR:000029187
name: ribosomal protein S6 kinase alpha
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that has a core domain composition consisting of a Protein kinase domain (Pfam:PF00069) followed by a Protein kinase C terminal domain (Pfam:PF00433) and another copy of the a Protein kinase domain (Pfam:PF00069). Prototype members of this class act downstream of ERK1/2 signaling pahtway. There are two functional kinase domains that are activated in a sequential manner by a series of phosphorylations." [PMID:10411321, PRO:CNA]
comment: Category=family.
synonym: "MAPK-activated protein kinase-1" EXACT [PMID:10411321]
synonym: "MAPKAP-K1" EXACT [PMID:10411321]
synonym: "p90 ribosomal S6 kinase" EXACT [PMID:19915011]
synonym: "p90RSK" EXACT [PMID:19915011]
synonym: "ribosomal protein S6 kinase II" EXACT [PIRSF:PIRSF000606]
xref: PIRSF:PIRSF000606
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

[Term]
id: PR:000029188
name: cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that has a core domain composition consisting of a Protein kinase domain (Pfam:PF00069). Prototype members of this class are the catalytic subunit of PKA. Protein Kinase A (PKA) catalyzes the transfer of the terminal phosphate of ATP to Thr or Ser residues in a variety of protein substrates. The enzyme is composed of two subunit types: a catalytic subunit and a regulatory subunit. In the absence of cAMP, the two subunits are bound to each other and no catalysis can take place. In the presence of cAMP, the regulatory subunit binds cAMP, thus releasing the catalytic subunit." [PMID:20188216, PRO:CNA]
comment: Category=family.
synonym: "cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit alpha/beta/gamma" EXACT [PIRSF:PIRSF501114]
synonym: "PKA" RELATED []
synonym: "PKA C" EXACT []
xref: PIRSF:PIRSF501114
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

[Term]
id: PR:000029189
name: AKT kinase
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that has a core domain composition consisting of a PH domain (Pfam:PF00169), Protein kinase domain (Pfam:PF00069) and a Protein kinase C terminal domain (Pfam:PF00433). Mammals have three genes encoding AKT1, AKT2 and AKT3. The second messenger phosphatidylinositol-3,4,5-trisphosphate [PIP(3)], product of phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase, acts largely through its role as a kinase activator. Binding of the pleckstrin domain to PIP(3) results in its targeting to the plasma membrane. Full activity is gained only after phosphorylation at two sites." [PMID:9736715, PRO:CNA]
comment: Category=family.
synonym: "AKT" EXACT []
synonym: "PKB" BROAD [PRO:DNx]
synonym: "serine-threonine kinase Akt" EXACT []
is_a: PR:000000001 ! protein

[Term]
id: PR:000029191
name: cyclin-related protein
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that consists of a copy of the Cyclin, N-terminal domain (Pfam:PF00134). This class includes the G1/S cyclins, essential for the control of the cell cycle at the G1/S transition, and the G2/M cyclins, essential for the control of the cell cycle at the G2/M transition." [PRO:CNA, PRO:DAN, Wikipedia:Cyclin]
comment: Category=family.
synonym: "fam:cyclin" EXACT PRO-short-label [PRO:DAN]
