[Term]
id: PR:000044371
name: dynamin-1 isoform ac
namespace: protein
def: "A dynamin-1 that is a translation product of some mRNA whose exon structure and start site selection renders it capable of giving rise to a protein with the amino acid sequence represented by UniProtKB:P21575-3 or a 1:1 ortholog thereof. This isoform contains the a version of the first splice region, and the c version of the second splice region." [PMID:17525220, PMID:9725914, PRO:KRC]
comment: Category=sequence. Note: PMID:9725914 describes two splicing regions for dynamin-1. The first splicing region of Dyn 1 contains either one of two sequences (a and b forms) of identical size but distinct nucleotide sequences. The second one is the region coding the C-terminus making at least four distinct tails for Dynamin-1. These consist of an a tail of 20 amino acids, a b tail of 7 amino acids, a c tail of 49 amino acids, and a d tail of 12 amino acids.
synonym: "DNM1/iso:ac" EXACT PRO-short-label [PRO:DNx]
synonym: "Dyn1ac" EXACT []
is_a: PR:000006601 ! dynamin-1

[Term]
id: PR:000044372
name: dynamin-1 isoform ac (mouse)
namespace: protein
def: "A dynamin-1 isoform ac that is encoded in the genome of mouse." [PMID:17525220, PRO:KRC, UniProtKB:F6W8Z8]
comment: Category=organism-sequence. Note: PMID:17525220 shows sequence of the ac isoform (nomenclature after the rat nomenclature from PMID:9725914). UniProtKB:F6W8Z8 sequence fragment provides additional experimental support for the existence of the c variant of the C-terminal of the two locations of alternative splicing in Dynamin-1. Note that this fragment sequence is equally consistent with the bc isoform since it contains only the C-terminal section containing only the second of two locations of alternative splicing.
synonym: "Dyn1ac (mouse)" EXACT []
synonym: "mDNM1/iso:ac" EXACT PRO-short-label [PRO:DNx]
