[Term]
id: PR:000045383
name: protein kinase C, iota-like
namespace: protein
def: "A protein that is a member of the phorbol ester (and diacylglycerol) receptor/protein kinase class. The canonical protein sequence has a core domain architecture consisting of a copy of the PB1 domain (Pfam:PF:00564), a Phorbol esters/diacylglycerol binding domain (C1 domain) (Pfam:PF00130), a Protein kinase domain (Pfam:PF00069) and a Protein kinase C terminal domain (Pfam:PF00433)." [PMID:8226978]
