[Term]
id: PR:A9P557
name: granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor receptor subunit alpha isoform 2 (mouse)
namespace: protein
def: "A granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor receptor subunit alpha (mouse) that is a translation product of some mRNA whose exon structure and start site selection renders it capable of giving rise to a protein with the amino acid sequence represented by UniProtKB:A9P557. This isoform lacks part of the Fibronectin type-III (PS50853) domain." [GenBank:EF114317, GenPept:ABO38428, PMID:17694571, PRO:HJD]
comment: Category=organism-sequence. Evidence=(ECO:0000006, based on PMID:17694571, at protein level). Note: PMID:17694571 shows that this isoform may be produced from a transcript where skipping of the splice acceptor of exon 6 and aberrant splicing into the coding sequence of exon 6 occurs.
synonym: "GM-CSF receptor alpha subunit isoform 2 (mouse)" EXACT []
synonym: "GM-CSF receptor alpha-chain isoform 2 (mouse)" EXACT []
synonym: "GMRalpha isoform 2 (mouse)" EXACT []
synonym: "mCSF2RA/iso:2" EXACT PRO-short-label [PRO:DNx]
xref: UniProtKB:A9P557
