[Term]
id: PR:Q2VEB4
name: A-kinase anchor protein 6 isoform alpha (mouse)
namespace: protein
def: "An A-kinase anchor protein 6 (mouse) that is a translation product of some mRNA whose exon structure and start site selection renders it capable of giving rise to a protein with the amino acid sequence represented by UniProtKB:Q2VEB4." [PMID:16337591, PRO:KRC]
comment: Category=organism-sequence. Evidence=(ECO:0000006, based on PMID:16337591, at mRNA and protein levels). Note: PMID:16337591 identifies mAKAP-alpha mRNA in mouse brain and a protein of 280kD by Western blot. The sequence Q2VEB4 has a few sequence conflicts when compared to the reference genome sequence. The difference could be due to different mouse strains.
