def: "A cell adhesion molecule CEACAM1 sequence variant CEACAM1b (mouse) that is a translation product of some mRNA whose exon structure and start site selection renders it capable of giving rise to a protein with the amino acid sequence represented by UniProtKB:Q61352. This form contains the four copies of the Ig domain and is the version with longer cytoplasmic tail." [PMID:10491101, PMID:11483763, PMID:7628460, PRO:KRC]
comment: Category=organism-sequence. Evidence=(ECO:0000006, based on PMID:7628460, at mRNA level). Note: PMID:10491101 and PMID:11483763 provide systematic nomenclatures.
